{"id":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch07_RicciCurvatureComparison#rem:pet-ch7-ex-16","title":"rem:pet-ch7-ex-16","path":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch07_RicciCurvatureComparison.md","line":720,"body":"","kind":"other","status":"not_started","tex":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch07_RicciCurvatureComparison.tex#rem:pet-ch7-ex-16","uses":["[[references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch07_RicciCurvatureComparison#rem:pet-ch7-ex-15]]","[[references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch07_RicciCurvatureComparison#thm:pet-ch7-cheng-rigidity]]"],"inspired_by":[],"bindings":[],"is_index":false,"body_html":"","formal":[],"tex_content":{"path":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch07_RicciCurvatureComparison.tex","label":"rem:pet-ch7-ex-16","line":1146,"source":"\\begin{remark}[Obata rigidity]\n  \\label{rem:pet-ch7-ex-16}\n\n  \\source{petersen:page-0324}\n  \\uses{rem:pet-ch7-ex-15, thm:pet-ch7-cheng-rigidity}\n  \\dcref{ch7:7.5.16}\n  Let $(M^n,g)$ be closed with $\\Ric\\ge(n-1)k>0$. Using the Bochner formula as\n  in \\cref{rem:pet-ch7-ex-15}, show that if $\\Delta u=-nk\\,u$ for some\n  function $u$, then $\\Hess u=-ku\\,g$. Conclude $(M^n,g)=S^n_k$.\n\\end{remark}","html":" <p></p><section class=\"theorem\"><div class=\"theorem-label\">Remark</div></section>[Obata rigidity] <span class=\"tex-label\" id=\"tex-label-72656d3a7065742d6368372d65782d3136\"></span> <p></p><span class=\"tex-source\" style=\"display:block\">Source: <span class=\"reference\">petersen:page-0324</span></span> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FPetersen%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh07_RicciCurvatureComparison%23rem%3Apet-ch7-ex-15\">↗ rem:pet-ch7-ex-15</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FPetersen%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh07_RicciCurvatureComparison%23thm%3Apet-ch7-cheng-rigidity\">↗ thm:pet-ch7-cheng-rigidity</a> <span class=\"tex-source-references\" role=\"list\" style=\"display:block\"><span class=\"tex-dcref\" role=\"listitem\" style=\"display:block\">1. ch7:7.5.16</span></span>Let <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$(M^n,g)$\">$(M^n,g)$</span> be closed with <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\Ric \\ge (n-1)k&gt;0$\">$\\Ric \\ge (n-1)k&gt;0$</span>. Using the Bochner formula as in <a class=\"reference tex-ref\" href=\"#node=references%2FPetersen%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh07_RicciCurvatureComparison%23rem%3Apet-ch7-ex-15\" data-tex-node=\"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch07_RicciCurvatureComparison#rem:pet-ch7-ex-15\" data-tex-anchor=\"tex-label-72656d3a7065742d6368372d65782d3135\">item 3</a>, show that if <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\Delta u=-nk\\, u$\">$\\Delta u=-nk\\, u$</span> for some function <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$u$\">$u$</span>, then <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\Hess u=-ku\\, g$\">$\\Hess u=-ku\\, g$</span>. Conclude <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$(M^n,g)=S^n_k$\">$(M^n,g)=S^n_k$</span>. ","warnings":[]},"previous":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch07_RicciCurvatureComparison#rem:pet-ch7-ex-15","next":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch07_RicciCurvatureComparison#rem:pet-ch7-ex-17","relations":[{"kind":"uses","id":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch07_RicciCurvatureComparison#rem:pet-ch7-ex-15","title":"rem:pet-ch7-ex-15","label":"rem:pet-ch7-ex-15"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch07_RicciCurvatureComparison#thm:pet-ch7-cheng-rigidity","title":"thm:pet-ch7-cheng-rigidity","label":"thm:pet-ch7-cheng-rigidity"}],"backlinks":[],"copy_context":{"version":1,"level":0,"node":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch07_RicciCurvatureComparison#rem:pet-ch7-ex-16","title":"rem:pet-ch7-ex-16","tex":"\\begin{remark}[Obata rigidity]\n  \\label{rem:pet-ch7-ex-16}\n\n  \\source{petersen:page-0324}\n  \\uses{rem